## PR Title
Deassert pcpi_valid upon asserting sbreak IRQ

## PR Description
Addresses issue #8 (incorrect handling of SBREAK / illegal instructions when PCPI is enabled): on `sbreak` / illegal instruction the core now deasserts `pcpi_valid` when raising the SBREAK IRQ, so the next valid PCPI instruction is not mis-flagged as another `sbreak`.

The author notes two remaining considerations:
1. Instructions like `sbreak` take roughly 16 cycles to trigger an IRQ because of PCPI timeout delays; immediate IRQ triggering for these instructions could be useful, though external PCPI modules might handle it differently.
2. The behaviour of `sbreak` or illegal instructions inside ISRs is not examined here, although trapping seems like the natural answer.

